  "text_input": "Patient is a 20-year-old male who presented with a 15-day history of cough, occasional with white mucoid expectoration and chest pain. Symptoms exacerbated over the last 4 days with continuous low-grade fever, sore throat, headache, and 3 episodes of non-bilious vomiting. Past history includes atopy (inhaler use until age 17) and recurrent tonsillitis. Physical examination revealed a blood pressure of 200/140 mmHg and pulse of 90 bpm. Systemic examination was largely normal. Investigations showed erythrocytosis and absolute neutrophilia on CBC, and Grade 1 fatty liver on USG. 2D Echo was normal with an EF of 62%. Diagnosed with acute bronchitis and acute pharyngitis with grade 1 tonsillitis. Treated with antibiotics (Tufzone, Azee), analgesics (Calpol), and nebulization.",
